-- The 12-module business curriculum as a Lattice course, structure only:
-- one course and twelve units, one per module, in dependency order. No
-- challenges, lessons or questions, because the content is not written yet.
--
-- Unpublished (is_published = 0): course.php, challenge.php, score-report.php
-- and home.php all require is_published = 1, so no student can see or reach
-- it. Publish it from /lattice/admin/courses.php once the content exists.
--
-- Titles and order follow hypnosis/website/includes/curriculum.php; every
-- description is drawn from writer/bizorca-curriculum.md (the authority on
-- what each module is). Ids are not hard-coded: the course is found by its
-- slug, and each row is skipped if it already exists, so this cannot collide
-- with "Personal Finance Fundamentals" (course 1) or anything added in the
-- admin. One statement per line, as bin/migrate.php splits on line-ending ';'.

INSERT INTO lt_courses (title, slug, description, thumbnail_path, is_published) SELECT 'The Business Curriculum', 'business-curriculum', 'Twelve modules, one system installed per module, each leaving a working artifact in the business afterward. Written for practitioners running their own practice: health and wellness providers, coaches, consultants, and tax professionals. The modules are ordered by dependency, not by domain. Module 8 works because module 1 happened, so take them in order. Modules 3, 8, and 9 (the offer, the price increase, and the delegation) are where owners reliably stall, and the obstacle there is behavioral, not informational.', '', 0 FROM DUAL WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lt_courses WHERE slug = 'business-curriculum');
INSERT INTO lt_units (course_id, sort_order, title, about_html, tutorials_url, is_final) SELECT c.id, 1, 'Module 1: Money Baseline', '<p>You can’t fix what you can’t see, and most owners have never seen it. This module establishes the true financial picture before any decisions get made against it: personal separated from business, the cash position and the fixed monthly burn, an honest break-even that includes the owner’s actual time, and what the owner really takes home.</p><p><strong>Artifact:</strong> A one-page financial baseline: cash position, break-even, and true owner pay.</p>', NULL, 0 FROM lt_courses c WHERE c.slug = 'business-curriculum' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lt_units u WHERE u.course_id = c.id AND u.sort_order = 1);
INSERT INTO lt_units (course_id, sort_order, title, about_html, tutorials_url, is_final) SELECT c.id, 2, 'Module 2: The Owner’s Time Audit', '<p>Gerber’s three roles, applied to an actual week. Track two weeks of real time, not remembered time, sort every hour into technician, manager, or entrepreneur, and name what only the owner can do and what has simply never been handed off.</p><p><strong>Artifact:</strong> The time audit, with the three-way split and the first candidate for removal.</p>', NULL, 0 FROM lt_courses c WHERE c.slug = 'business-curriculum' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lt_units u WHERE u.course_id = c.id AND u.sort_order = 2);
INSERT INTO lt_units (course_id, sort_order, title, about_html, tutorials_url, is_final) SELECT c.id, 3, 'Module 3: The One Offer', '<p>Most marketing problems are offer problems. This module narrows the offer to something describable in a sentence, written as the buyer would describe it, priced against real capacity and overhead rather than competitors, and bounded by what gets declined.</p><p><strong>Artifact:</strong> The written offer and the pricing rationale behind it.</p>', NULL, 0 FROM lt_courses c WHERE c.slug = 'business-curriculum' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lt_units u WHERE u.course_id = c.id AND u.sort_order = 3);
INSERT INTO lt_units (course_id, sort_order, title, about_html, tutorials_url, is_final) SELECT c.id, 4, 'Module 4: Lead Flow', '<p>One channel, built to work, rather than five channels dabbled in. The channel is chosen by a question: does the buyer know they have this problem before they meet you? If not, it is workshop-led. If so, it is referral-led. Build one, measure it, and leave the others alone until this one produces.</p><p><strong>Artifact:</strong> One documented acquisition channel with a defined weekly action.</p>', NULL, 0 FROM lt_courses c WHERE c.slug = 'business-curriculum' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lt_units u WHERE u.course_id = c.id AND u.sort_order = 4);
INSERT INTO lt_units (course_id, sort_order, title, about_html, tutorials_url, is_final) SELECT c.id, 5, 'Module 5: The Sales Conversation', '<p>The gap between an interested prospect and a paying client is usually a conversation nobody planned. This module makes it repeatable: the conversation mapped from first contact to signed agreement, the qualifying and disqualifying questions, the price objection handled before it arrives, and a follow-up sequence, since most sales are lost to silence rather than to no.</p><p><strong>Artifact:</strong> A documented conversation structure and a written follow-up sequence.</p>', NULL, 0 FROM lt_courses c WHERE c.slug = 'business-curriculum' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lt_units u WHERE u.course_id = c.id AND u.sort_order = 5);
INSERT INTO lt_units (course_id, sort_order, title, about_html, tutorials_url, is_final) SELECT c.id, 6, 'Module 6: Delivery Documented', '<p>If you handed this to someone else next month, what would they need? This module writes the delivery process down step by step, in the order it happens, including the decisions the owner makes without thinking, which are the hardest to hand off and the most valuable to record.</p><p><strong>Artifact:</strong> The task library: the delivery process written down as a working document.</p>', NULL, 0 FROM lt_courses c WHERE c.slug = 'business-curriculum' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lt_units u WHERE u.course_id = c.id AND u.sort_order = 6);
INSERT INTO lt_units (course_id, sort_order, title, about_html, tutorials_url, is_final) SELECT c.id, 7, 'Module 7: Collections Cadence', '<p>Revenue that never arrives isn’t revenue. Short on theory and long on the specific discomfort of asking for money: invoice timing that isn’t a decision each time, a written follow-up sequence, terms the owner will actually enforce, and the current aging list worked before the month is out.</p><p><strong>Artifact:</strong> The collections calendar and a cleared backlog.</p>', NULL, 0 FROM lt_courses c WHERE c.slug = 'business-curriculum' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lt_units u WHERE u.course_id = c.id AND u.sort_order = 7);
INSERT INTO lt_units (course_id, sort_order, title, about_html, tutorials_url, is_final) SELECT c.id, 8, 'Module 8: The Price Increase', '<p>Executed, not contemplated. This is where the earlier work pays for itself, and where behavioral resistance shows up most reliably. The new price is set against the module 3 rationale and the module 1 numbers, the client communication is written, and then it gets sent.</p><p><strong>Artifact:</strong> The increase in effect, with the communication sent.</p>', NULL, 0 FROM lt_courses c WHERE c.slug = 'business-curriculum' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lt_units u WHERE u.course_id = c.id AND u.sort_order = 8);
INSERT INTO lt_units (course_id, sort_order, title, about_html, tutorials_url, is_final) SELECT c.id, 9, 'Module 9: First Delegation', '<p>One role, defined and handed off. Not a hiring plan, but a single transfer that proves the task library works: the task with the highest hours and the lowest required judgment, defined against what module 6 documented, with a clear picture of what done looks like and how it gets checked.</p><p><strong>Artifact:</strong> One role defined, documented, and transferred.</p>', NULL, 0 FROM lt_courses c WHERE c.slug = 'business-curriculum' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lt_units u WHERE u.course_id = c.id AND u.sort_order = 9);
INSERT INTO lt_units (course_id, sort_order, title, about_html, tutorials_url, is_final) SELECT c.id, 10, 'Module 10: The Owner’s Dashboard', '<p>Five numbers, reviewed weekly: trailing 90-day cash flow, fixed monthly burn, pipeline or booked work ahead, receivables aging, and one number specific to this business. Tax-return accounting is historical, and operating decisions are forward-looking.</p><p><strong>Artifact:</strong> The dashboard, with a standing weekly review on the calendar.</p>', NULL, 0 FROM lt_courses c WHERE c.slug = 'business-curriculum' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lt_units u WHERE u.course_id = c.id AND u.sort_order = 10);
INSERT INTO lt_units (course_id, sort_order, title, about_html, tutorials_url, is_final) SELECT c.id, 11, 'Module 11: Tax and Entity Hygiene', '<p>The regulatory layer, addressed once a year rather than discovered in a letter: entity structure reviewed against the current stage, the estimated payment schedule set and funded from module 1’s allocation, worker classification and licensing checked, and what belongs with a CPA identified before year-end rather than after.</p><p><strong>Artifact:</strong> A structure review and a funded quarterly schedule.</p>', NULL, 0 FROM lt_courses c WHERE c.slug = 'business-curriculum' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lt_units u WHERE u.course_id = c.id AND u.sort_order = 11);
INSERT INTO lt_units (course_id, sort_order, title, about_html, tutorials_url, is_final) SELECT c.id, 12, 'Module 12: The Annual Plan', '<p>One page. Everything installed across the year, turned into what happens next: the one constraint that limits growth right now, three targets with dates and numbers attached, what gets stopped (a plan without subtraction is a wish list), and the quarterly reviews that keep it alive.</p><p><strong>Artifact:</strong> The next twelve months on a single page.</p>', NULL, 0 FROM lt_courses c WHERE c.slug = 'business-curriculum' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM lt_units u WHERE u.course_id = c.id AND u.sort_order = 12);
